WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:03.759
Good morning, John, this is what I'm planning
on wearing to your movie premiere. I don't

00:00:03.759 --> 00:00:08.519
know, is it too much? Is it not enough? I
don't know. Coming all the way from Montana,

00:00:08.519 --> 00:00:11.900
show those New York people a thing or two
about how people should dress: you know, with

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:15.860
a dead cow on them. Check out the tie: TFiOS
colors tie.

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:22.860
John, we have officially received over 100,000
responses to the 2014 Nerdfighteria Census.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:28.370
Which is even more exciting because over half
of the 140,000 that responded last year didn't

00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:32.680
respond this year. I don't know what those
people were doing; there's 100,000 of them.

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:35.870
Maybe they figured they'd do one census, but
I should wait four years or so before I do

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:39.660
another one, right? But, it's not because
people weren't around last year because 75%

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:43.700
of respondents have been watching since before
2013. That's a lot of long-time nerdfighters.

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:48.640
Other interesting data from the survey, 100%
of people say my new album Incongruent is

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:53.399
a masterful work of genius. It was the only
option I gave them, but still. Actually, a

00:00:53.399 --> 00:00:57.350
lot of people didn't even know that I have
a new album, so, I have a new album! In fact,

00:00:57.350 --> 00:01:00.180
there are a number of things we do that people
didn't know anything about.

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:03.469
14% of people don't know about the Mental
Floss channel where we're constantly spewing

00:01:03.469 --> 00:01:06.390
interesting facts about the world.
30% of people don't know that we've spun off

00:01:06.390 --> 00:01:10.610
SciShow into a second SciShow channel, so
there's SciShow and SciShow Space.

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:15.360
33% of people don't know about our year-old
YouTube sex education and information show

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:19.810
Sexplanations with Dr. Lindsey Doe.
50% of people don't know about How To Adult,

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:24.619
our guide to suddenly becoming an adult and
OH GOD OH GOD!

00:01:24.619 --> 00:01:29.650
64% of people don't know about our new show
Animal Wonders, but the number one most underground,

00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:35.650
super-indie, nobody knows about it thing that's
part of all of our enterprises is The Warehouse.

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:40.420
The Warehouse is a show that is produced out
of the DFTBA Records warehouse by Matthew

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:44.619
Gaydos, who is the head of Customer Service
at DFTBA Records. I actually watched him do

00:01:44.619 --> 00:01:48.750
a show at Sean Kelly's last night in Missoula.
He is a rock star.

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:53.130
Somewhat difficult for me to believe is that
40% of people don't know about Subbable. I

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:56.490
just feel like everybody knows about it because
it has been so successful for helping us fund

00:01:56.490 --> 00:02:01.680
our shows, like, SciShow and CrashCourse and
Sexplanations would all not exist any more

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:02.860
if it weren't for Subbable.

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:07.540
For those 40%of people who don't know, Subbable
is our voluntary subscription platform. You

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:12.540
can go and subscribe to any of a number of
projects, and when you subscribe you can choose

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:16.450
an amount to pay per month. And that can be
0 dollars, it could be 5 or 10, or a million

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:20.200
dollars a month. Nobody's done that yet. And
that helps those shows exist for everybody,

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:21.680
including people who can't pay for them.

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:24.730
Speaking of people who can't pay for them
-- in the comments of the questions about

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:28.270
Subbable and DFTBA and my album, there are
lots of people saying "I just don't have money,

00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:31.290
I feel really bad that I haven't bought your
things, but I don't have money..." Don't feel

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:37.030
bad. About that ever! That is the last thing
I want, is for you to spend money when it

00:02:37.030 --> 00:02:40.650
will make you less financially secure.
If you buy something from us and it's making

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:46.060
you less financially secure, I am not happy.
Don't do that. No.

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:50.830
And really astonishingly, 1) More people have
read J. K. Rowling books than have read John

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:56.700
Green books, but only very slightly. And something
like 92% of you have read The Fault in Our

00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:58.000
Stars, which is a lot.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:03.030
So I'm assuming that all of those people will
be interested in going to The Night Before

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:07.220
Our Stars. It's an event that's happening
all over America, not outside America, sorry

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:11.250
not-America people. Also not in everywhere
in America. Like it's not happening here in

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:11.930
Missoula for example.

00:03:11.930 --> 00:03:15.030
It's the screening of the movie, the day before
it comes out, on June 5th. 5:30 Eastern, 8:30

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:21.879
Pacific, I think. And then after the movie,
there's going to be a livestream of questions

00:03:21.879 --> 00:03:26.739
and interviews and music, with John Green:
my brother, the guy on the other side of this

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:32.519
camera. Nat Wolff, Ansel Elgort, Shailene
Woodley, Josh Boone: the director, other people.

00:03:32.519 --> 00:03:38.000
It's gonna be cool. You should check it out,
if you can. Sorry, very sorry, to all the

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:39.340
people who can't.

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:44.290
John, congratulations. Coming to your premiere!
Gonna get on a plane tomorrow and come see

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:46.930
you! Looking forward to it. I'll see you then.

00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:49.940
LeVar Burton: Though I have to say, Hank,
your video about how to field strip a fusion

00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:55.110
reactor or realign the power transfer tunnel
in a warp coil generator is lacking in the

00:03:55.110 --> 00:03:57.919
most rudimentary understanding of matter-antimatter
principles.

